      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "this is simply horrible. if you can't provide a slider that goes from off to whatever then it shouldn't exist, at all as it's a net negative. \n\nidk how the smoothing is achieved, but even with a constant speed movement it lags behind the tracker. this is not okay. we want to eliminate high frequency noise, not just average the last x samples as it currently *looks* (and feels). please investigate the Kalman filter, or something similar for this.\n\nI agree with others, there is already a steamvr plugin for this that's better at this.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "64c6b85269fa9f0984977a0b",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f4d0c8c4efb1c1bee087245",
        "alias": "Tawny Aardvark",
        "aliasID": "65c2892ded6eefce4ca818ef",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/c03c152b315f5f0d0ed8998a48811438.png",
        "created": "2020-08-31T14:43:24.515Z",
        "name": "Guribo",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "guribo-1"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "621946996d11764c11ffcf01",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-07-30T19:21:54.659Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64c2d02c35fe7609581319ae",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I compared the way it behaves to the Smoothtracking tool for SteamVR and to me it looks like VRC does exactly the same: it turns off tracking prediction. In a nutshell we get the actual recorded positions without any prediction by steamvr, this makes them effectively lag behind our real limbs but eliminates any possible noise caused by false predictions.\n\nPersonally I would only like to have it on feet and hip but not on controllers, controllers are being tracked really well including steamvrs prediction. Games like shooters or any kind of game that requires snappy input are almost unplayable with the additional delay caused by lack of prediction... So either a toggle or sliders for the various tracking devices would be nice, just like Smoothtracking already has in SteamVR.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "64c75e5ccf63f909455d68c5",
      "author": {
        "_id": "62e16b60fe86b444ae593a33",
        "alias": "Clean Dragonfly",
        "aliasID": "663ba2bcd36452c1796552b6",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/bd1f53b648f2abc1d125a5181894d470.png",
        "created": "2022-07-27T16:44:16.115Z",
        "name": "Limblicious",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "limblicious"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "621946996d11764c11ffcf01",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-07-31T07:10:20.586Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64c2d02c35fe7609581319ae",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would also like enable/disable or sliders for controllers and trackers.\n\nI believe this is the third party app people are referring to when talking about motion smoothing/jitter reduction for trackers: https://booth.pm/ja/items/4018006. I've been using this for quite some time. \n\nAs far as I can tell both the new IK in the beta and this app do the same thing, trade tracker positional lag for reduced tracker jitter. In my experience this is not actually ideal for dancing, because a lot of small technical movements or quick movements get muted/deleted/nerfed by the motion smoothing. This issue is exacerbated over the network when I am watching friends use this app with the movement smoothing maxed out, they almost look like they're barely moving at all if they have max smoothing.\n\nI was hoping that the VRC beta IK kept that raw movement input and still sent that over the network so that as much movement is shown to other players but after dancing today...I don't think that's the case.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "64c7e3b95ba05d2e647e1f9b",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f38466a3ea8727b74c9de69",
        "alias": "Eburnean Camel",
        "aliasID": "65c30a82ed6eefce4cc09698",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/2ea13c0d28407c4b299b5d63562ae89b.png",
        "created": "2020-08-15T20:32:42.881Z",
        "name": "Dearsren",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "dearsren"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "621946996d11764c11ffcf01",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-07-31T16:39:21.126Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64c2d02c35fe7609581319ae",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "with the tracker jitter correction i can clearly feel and see my avatars legs dragging behind my trackers.\n\ni don't like that delay at all and prefer responsiveness. It feels very off and immersion breaking for me. Some people are may not as sensitive to delay than me or prefer the reduced jitter despite the added delay. But tbh i dont really want to use it as it is now.\n\nThe delay isn't as bad on the hands. I notice it on elbows and knee's too but on the feet trackers it's the worst.\n\nIt would be great if the reduced jitter could be achieved without the delay. Or if there would be a toggle to turn this function off or a slider to adjust how much the jitter gets reduced so everyone could adjust it to their likings.\n\nIt would also be okay for me if there would be a launch argument to disable it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
